Task: Wire order.status-changed into StockEventConsumer.reservationFailedStream (US-5.4, Phase 2 part 2)

Summary: Added publishStatusChangedIfUpdated helper (mirrors
publishReservedIfUpdated from US-5.3), wired into reservationFailedStream via
.flatTap after a successful updateStatusByItemId transition. run[F] now
passes the publisher to both streams (reservedStream already had it from
US-5.3). reservedStream itself is unchanged - it still only publishes
order.reserved, never order.status-changed.

Flaky test found and fixed (not a production bug): the new positive test
("...also publishes order.status-changed...") used consumeOne - grab the
first message ever on the topic - which is unsafe once more than one test in
this shared-Testcontainers-Kafka suite can publish to the same topic
concurrently with a real (non-noOp) publisher. Replaced consumeOne with a
new consumeMatching helper that filters by this test's own order id, same
robustness fix already applied to the negative test pattern in US-5.3's
track. Also retrofitted US-5.3's own analogous "also publishes order.reserved"
test to use consumeMatching instead of consumeOne, since it has the exact
same latent vulnerability (just hadn't been observed failing yet) - removed
the now-dead consumeOne helper entirely. Confirmed stable across 3 repeated
full-suite runs after the fix (8/8 each time), whereas it failed roughly half
the time before.

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/StockEventConsumer.scala
  (publishStatusChangedIfUpdated, reservationFailedStream, run)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/StockEventConsumerSuite.scala
  (consumeMatching replaces consumeOne; 2 new tests: publishes on
  reservation-failed with correct fields, never publishes from reservedStream)

Tests: 116 passed, 0 failed (full suite, confirmed stable across repeats).

Why: this is the second of the two failure paths order-service needs to
publish from - the async path, mirroring the synchronous OrderRoutes path
wired in the previous task. Together they close the gap this whole track
exists to fix.
